From 4b14b4bf3e627946a162ca8ae4a6b406c77a7aa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Owen Phillips <ophilli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:32:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fall back to the .json.zip NVD feed when .json.gz gives 404
 (#183)

After NVD rewrites a feed, the .json.gz file can return 404 for some
minutes while the .json.zip copy of the same feed is already served.
With a cache less than 7 days old, vulnix loads only the "modified"
feed, so this one missing file made every scan fail.

On a 404 for the .json.gz file, Archive.download() now requests the
.json.zip file and reads the one JSON file in it. A 404 for both still
raises HTTPError.

A feed from one URL can be older than the feed loaded before from the
other URL. Meta now saves each feed's top-level "timestamp", and an
older .gz or .zip feed is skipped without saving its ETag. When a feed
is accepted, the other URL's ETag is removed, so a switch between
formats gets a full response for the age check. This also covers
caches from before this change.

Requires Python 3.11+ for datetime.fromisoformat() to parse NVD's
7-digit fractional seconds.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
